  "rationale": "**Holds.** `dispatch_builtin`: `PreToolUse` -> `OutputEvent::empty_for(PreToolUse)`. `PostToolUse` / `UserPromptSubmit` -> `possible_new_plugins_notice`, which is empty unless `notify` (the new-plugins notice). Every other non-`SessionStart` event (`Stop`) -> `empty_for(input.event())`. The earlier bug where `Stop` got a `PreToolUse`-shaped output is fixed.\n\n**Tests (all pass):** `hook::tests::builtin_pre_tool_use_returns_empty`, `builtin_post_tool_use_returns_empty_when_dependencies_are_unchanged`, `builtin_user_prompt_submit_returns_empty_when_dependencies_are_unchanged`, `builtin_stop_returns_an_empty_stop_output` (asserts an `OutputEvent::Stop` with no context), `symposium_output_empty_has_no_context`. `tests/plugin_notice.rs::a_dependency_added_by_a_tool_call_is_noticed_once` shows later `PostToolUse` / `UserPromptSubmit` events carry no notice once deps are unchanged.\n",
  "requirement": "Except for the new-plugins notice, Symposium's built-in handling MUST add no context on events other than `SessionStart`."
}
